From 8c6ca1beb76d57e06ba48d111612da3af399f148 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 22:01:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] fix: ratchet the commit blend, and give the policy the
 ratchet's state

S8. The gain calibration T10 section 7 asked for cannot be done: the blend
spans a geometrically fixed 13 m of commanded radius -- the hold freezes at
12-19 m against a desired pose at 3 m -- so warping it only moves where the
6.5 m per unit of action sits, and a rate limit sized to the 0.094 m a chaser
covers in one decision needs 138 decisions to reach the commit, 276 s of a
300 s episode. The traces show oscillation rather than travel: dead seeds walk
a_commit up and down and spend the authority reversing, while every completing
episode rises once and pins.

So the factor is a ratchet, b_k = max(b_{k-1}, b_k_commanded). No tunable
constant, a commit still reachable in one decision, holding available for as
long as the policy keeps a_commit low, and every commit time the headroom sweep
found is a monotone hold-then-commit, so no measured headroom is removed.

Measured without training, by injecting the dead seeds' own action statistics --
a_commit ~ N(0.80, 0.09) -- into the eight seeds the fixed setpoint completes.
Raw blend: 0 of 8, a 0.618 m median waypoint step against 0.094 m of authority,
and 1792 to 2162 N s of fuel against a 173 N s baseline. Ratcheted: 7 of 8, and
the median step returns to 0.000 m. That also settles the interface-gain claim
T7_T9_REVIEW section 5 flagged as inference with no experiment, and it settles
it more cheaply than the retraining that review asked for.

The bitwise floor is intact: a = (+1, *) over twelve seeds reproduces the
pre-ratchet commit_now run with zero field mismatches and no fuel difference at
all, because max(b, 1.0) = 1.0 makes the ratchet the identity at that corner.

The ratchet carries state between decisions, so the same action commands
different waypoints depending on how far the commit has advanced. Without that
state in the observation the problem is no longer Markov and the policy would
be guessing at its own past, so the blend level is appended as one scalar in
[0, 1]: 24D to 25D under arrival_condition with the ratchet, unchanged
otherwise, first 24 dimensions bitwise identical. It is not a second factor --
without it the ratchet is not trainable.

--no-monotone-commit is the ablation switch and the manifest records it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
