From 07d622a674a314276fb344ecabb6b61237915a12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 00:57:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] docs: T12 execution order -- both gates passed, start the
 training round

Six training runs, three seeds each on arrival_condition and radial_local, all
from zero, then evaluation over the 48-seed block and the main table.

Flags the one parameter that would silently void the round: train_hybrid's
--horizon defaults to 20 while every T10 and T11 number -- the 48-seed
baseline, the six-point commit sweep, the 192-episode reverse cost -- was
measured at h35. It also explains why horizon 35 against a 20-step reference
hold is not the transparency trap it looks like: the whole line was measured in
that configuration, and its commit_now h35 row reproduces PURE_MPC_ROW_VERIFIED
exactly, which was produced through a different reference path entirely.

Also pins --no-execution-feedback, which is not the default, and records that
the ratchet is on by default with --no-monotone-commit reserved for a later
ablation rather than the main row.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KfdW4y9TEkhu2Sc1bKnkER
